# ISO 9241-110 interaction

## 7.6 Error tolerance
- Validate on blur and before submit. Disable submit while in-flight (no double submit).
- Wrap route/app UI in error boundaries; failures must not wipe the whole shell.
- Microcopy is non-technical. Every error has a recovery: retry, fix field, saved draft, or undo where data was mutated.
- Destructive actions need confirm. Overrides (materials/payment) stay explicit and audited.

## 7.2 Self-descriptiveness
- Async work shows status immediately: skeleton or spinner, then result. Prefer optimistic UI only when rollback is defined.
- Empty, loading, success, and error are distinct views. Never a blank panel.

## 7.5 Controllability
- Full keyboard and touch paths. Esc/cancel stops long requests where the server allows.
- User can abandon a form without data loss when a draft exists (orders, measurements).

## 7.3 Conformity with expectations
- Same tokens, spacing scale, type, and patterns everywhere (buttons, tables, toasts).
- Primary action is one per view. Status labels match the domain (`CONFIRMED`, not “OK”).

## 7.1 Suitability for the task
- Shop-floor: few taps to start/complete a task. Sales: no re-typing customer/phone/measurement.
- Do not add fields, steps, or decoration that do not serve the current job.
